.\" The manual page of the command line and both windows,
.\" which dog-vision-common installs and the packages of the three commands link to under each command's name.
.\" Each command lists its own options with --help, which this page leaves to it.
.TH DOG-VISION 1 "" "dog-vision" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
dog-vision-cli, dog-vision-compose, dog-vision-swing \- how a dog or another animal sees colours
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dog-vision-cli
[\fIoptions\fR] \fIfile\fR
.br
.B dog-vision-compose
[\fIoptions\fR] [\fIfile\fR]
.br
.B dog-vision-swing
[\fIoptions\fR] [\fIfile\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
dog-vision shows a photo, a video or the camera
with the colours a dog, a cat or another animal can tell apart, beside the original.
.TP
.B dog-vision-cli
converts a photo or a video, given as \fIfile\fR, and writes the result beside it,
such as \fIphoto.dog.png\fR or \fIclip.dog.mp4\fR; it opens no window.
.TP
.BR dog-vision-compose ", " dog-vision-swing
are the same desktop window, in Compose and in Swing: the camera, or \fIfile\fR where one is given,
as the chosen animal sees it; they save snapshots and recordings into an output folder, and convert the file shown.
.SH OPTIONS
Each command lists its options with \fB\-\-help\fR: the animal, a second one to compare with,
a map of the differences, the strength of the simulation and the blur to the animal's acuity,
and the command's own, such as \fB\-\-output\-dir\fR.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.BR LANGUAGE ", " LC_ALL ", " LC_MESSAGES ", " LANG
the language the commands speak, English or Czech, as gettext reads them.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/dog-vision/settings.json
the windows' settings, such as the output folder; in \fI~/.config\fR where \fBXDG_CONFIG_HOME\fR is not set.
.SH NOTES
A video, and the camera in a window, need ffmpeg.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ffmpeg (1)
.PP
https://github.com/loplex/dog-vision
